Third-party code and tooling
----------------------------
Rust dependencies keep their own licenses (see Cargo.lock).

If code or substantial structure is ever taken from an open-source project
(for example IntelliJ Community / PyCharm Community, Apache-2.0), record it
in a file under notices/ with: source URL, commit, file(s), license, and what
was changed.

The full list of third-party notices is in the notices/ folder, one file per
entry. `python3 scripts/notice.py --out <file>` assembles the complete text
(this header, every entry, the trademarks) for distributions.

